        "details": "",
        "free": "On March 8, 1962, the Soviet Union and the United States extended the Lacy-Zarubin accord on American-Soviet cultural exchange. Two significant exhibitions were staged entitled 'Soviet Graphics' which toured the USA, and 'Graphic Arts: USA' which toured the U.S.S.R in 1963-64.  The latter was the second United States Information Agency exhibition to bring American visual arts and posters to a Soviet audience, touring Alma-Ata, Moscow, Leningrad (Saint Petersburg) and Yerevan.  Ivan Chermayeff, along with his business partner Thomas Geismar, selected some 1000 examples of American graphic art and also co-designed the layout of the show and created this exhibition poster.",
